{
  "id": "29106_kamikorosu",
  "headword": "{噛|か}み{殺|ころ}す",
  "reading": "かみころす",
  "romaji": "kamikorosu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to stifle; to suppress; to bite back",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to stifle; to suppress (a yawn, laugh, or impulse)",
      "explanation": "To suppress or hold back a physical or emotional response, especially a yawn or laugh. The image is of biting something to stop it from escaping."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29106_kamikorosu_ex1",
      "japanese": "あくびを{噛|か}み{殺|ころ}す。",
      "english": "To stifle a yawn.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29106_kamikorosu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{笑|わら}いを{噛|か}み{殺|ころ}して{真剣|しんけん}な{顔|かお}をした。",
      "english": "I suppressed a laugh and kept a serious face.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29106_kamikorosu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{退屈|たいくつ}な{会議|かいぎ}の{中|なか}で、{何度|なんど}もあくびを{噛|か}み{殺|ころ}さなければならなかった。",
      "english": "During the boring meeting, I had to stifle yawns many times.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound verb formed from {噛|か}む (to bite) + {殺|ころ}す (to kill/suppress). Used figuratively to mean holding back an involuntary response.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- あくびを{噛|か}み{殺|ころ}す: to stifle a yawn\n- {笑|わら}いを{噛|か}み{殺|ころ}す: to suppress a laugh\n- {怒|いか}りを{噛|か}み{殺|ころ}す: to suppress anger\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {抑|おさ}える: to hold back, to suppress — more general; can apply to emotions or physical actions\n- {堪|こら}える: to endure, to hold back — implies effort; used for tears, laughter, pain",
